From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 20:38:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Cannibalization gate: subtopic guard, stripMold cleanup,
 cluster consolidation
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Follow-up to the entity recalibration, from validation against the real corpus.

(C) Subtopic guard: besides numbered variants, entities where one is a strict
    subset of the other with a MEANINGFUL extra qualifier are distinct topics and
    never block ("estresse pós-traumático" vs "…no trabalho"; "avaliação para
    cirurgia" vs "…de catarata"; general vs "tipo 1"). A filler-only extra
    ("…sem motivo" vs "…sem motivo aparente") is NOT distinct and still blocks,
    so real rewordings keep being caught. saoTemasDistintos = number OR subtopic.

(D) stripMold cleanup: removes leftover connectives after mold removal (leading
    "google", border/adjacent stopword runs) so "de ansiedade generalizada" →
    "ansiedade generalizada", "burnout e para melhorar" → "burnout melhorar",
    while a single connective between content words is preserved ("não monogamia
    e poliamor"). Cosmetic; did not flip decisions but keeps entities clean.

(B) Consolidation (explicit decision = one dense post per theme, matching the
    gate): when a cluster post is published, the sibling questions pulled into its
    H2/FAQ are also marked `used` (marcarComoUsadas), so they don't return as
    separate targets the gate would later reject. Aligns the queue with the gate.

Report now returns `temasDistintos` (number or subtopic) driving `bloquearia`.
Typecheck + build pass.

