 ### Blog anti-cannibalization (semantic + lexical)
 - Problem it solves: the only duplicate guard used to be EXACT normalized-title match, which let heavy THEME cannibalization through (near-twin titles, clustered subcategorias). This adds real near-duplicate detection.
 - Additive schema: table `blog_post_index` (`lib/db/src/schema/blog-post-index.ts`) — `post_id` (PK, FK→blog_posts), `title_normalized`, `entity_normalized` (pg_trgm; title with the boilerplate mold stripped), `embedded_text`, `embedding` vector(1024) (pgvector, nullable), `updated_at`. Nothing else changes; `blog_keyword_queue` is untouched.
-- Two detection layers (`lib/corpus-index.ts`): Camada 1 lexical compares the ENTITY, not the whole title — `similarity(entity_normalized, stripMold(cand)) > BLOG_CANIB_LEX` (default 0.72, pg_trgm). Comparing full titles let distinct topics collide on the shared mold ("… tem cura? o que esperar do tratamento", "… o que é e como…"); `stripMold` removes those so "alcoolismo" vs "bulimia" ≈ 0. Camada 2 semantic cosine `> BLOG_CANIB_SEM` (default 0.90, pgvector). NUMBERED-VARIANT GUARD: entities equal except for a number (Bipolar Tipo 1 vs Tipo 2) are distinct topics and never block, in both layers. Both layers FAIL-OPEN: no table/extension or no embeddings → "not duplicate" (never blocks generation). Thresholds are env-tunable in prod without a logic redeploy.
+- Two detection layers (`lib/corpus-index.ts`): Camada 1 lexical compares the ENTITY, not the whole title — `similarity(entity_normalized, stripMold(cand)) > BLOG_CANIB_LEX` (default 0.72, pg_trgm). Comparing full titles let distinct topics collide on the shared mold ("… tem cura? o que esperar do tratamento", "… o que é e como…"); `stripMold` removes those so "alcoolismo" vs "bulimia" ≈ 0. Camada 2 semantic cosine `> BLOG_CANIB_SEM` (default 0.90, pgvector). DISTINCT-TOPIC GUARD (both layers never block): entities equal except for a number (Bipolar Tipo 1 vs Tipo 2), OR one entity a strict subset of the other with a meaningful extra qualifier (subtema: "estresse pós-traumático" vs "…no trabalho"; "avaliação psicológica para cirurgia" vs "…de catarata"). A filler-only extra ("…sem motivo" vs "…sem motivo aparente") is NOT a distinct topic and still blocks. `stripMold` also cleans leftover connectives so the entity is clean. Both layers FAIL-OPEN: no table/extension or no embeddings → "not duplicate" (never blocks generation). Thresholds are env-tunable in prod without a logic redeploy.
 - Two checkpoints (reusing the existing anchored flow): (1) ENQUEUE — `enfileirarSugestoes` skips a mined search already covered lexically; and `processarCategoriaComFila` skips a target already covered before generating. (2) BEFORE PUBLISH — `verificarCanibalizacao(title, excerpt)` (L1+L2) discards a draft too close to an existing post and marks the queue item `skipped` for human consolidation.
+- STRATEGY = one dense post per theme (consolidation), matching the gate: when a cluster post is published, its sibling questions pulled into H2/FAQ are ALSO marked `used` (`marcarComoUsadas`), so they don't come back as separate targets the gate would then reject (this aligns the queue with the gate). To instead cover distinct search intents as separate posts, that consolidation + the same-entity block would need to be relaxed (intent-aware) — a deliberate change, not the current default.
 - Cross-citation: `postsRelacionadosParaCitar` (semantic band [0.35, 0.85)) feeds related posts into `generatePostAncorado`, which cites 2-3 naturally via `[texto](/blog/slug)`. `sectionsToHtml(body, slugsPermitidos)` converts those to `<a>` ONLY for allowlisted slugs (others become plain text) — no broken internal links possible.
 - `persistGeneratedPost` (re)indexes the post via `indexarPost` right after publishing, keeping the corpus current.
 - Embeddings provider (`lib/embeddings.ts`, 1024 dims, fail-open, 15s timeout/attempt): the Replit OpenAI proxy does NOT route the embeddings API (documented unsupported), so precedence is: (1) `BLOG_EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=voyage`+key, (2) own key `BLOG_EMBEDDING_API_KEY` (+ optional `BLOG_EMBEDDING_BASE_URL`, default OpenAI) — RECOMMENDED, (3) the Replit proxy `AI_INTEGRATIONS_OPENAI_*` only as a last resort, with a one-time WARN. `BLOG_EMBEDDING_MODEL` overrides the model. Without any, only Camada 1 lexical runs.
